# An ALLOWLIST, not a denylist, because a denylist is one forgotten line away from baking a
# credential into an image. `exulanica/models/credentials.py` walks up from the process working
# directory looking for a `.env` file, so a `.env` that reaches /app is a credential the image
# carries, which `docs/deployment.md` forbids. It is excluded here structurally rather than by a
# rule somebody has to remember to add.
#
# It is also the difference between a build context of about 1.5 GB and one of a few megabytes:
# `.venv`, `web/node_modules`, `.orimera` and `.exulanica` are the bulk of this checkout and the
# image needs none of them.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!LICENSE
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
!exulanica
# The piece formats the package imports, a second top-level package of the same wheel.
!exulanica_pieces
# The published material catalog, without the texture blobs: what the API needs to check a
# person's recipe against the published makers. About 200 KiB.
!assets/textures/manifest.json
!assets/textures/catalog.json
!assets/textures/objects
!assets/textures/blobs
# The versioned catalogs the package reads, some of them when it is imported: the society's
# routine, words and identities, and the detector's vocabulary. About 800 KiB.
!assets/catalogs
# The committed style pack library the API serves, read and checked when it starts. About 520 KiB.
!assets/style-packs
# The character catalogs the image publishes, with their containers and licences. About 22 MB.
!assets/characters/catalog.json
!assets/characters/looks.json
!assets/characters/parametric-catalog.json
!assets/characters/makehuman-people-v1
!assets/characters/makehuman-parametric-v1
# The installation profiles an installation names (docs/deployment.md 9.1).
!deploy/profiles
# The gsplat trainer recipe under deploy/gsplat is its own build; it needs only its pinned
# requirements from this directory.
!deploy/gsplat/requirements.txt
